    "chunk_size_bytes": 2017,
    "chunk_text": "(3) In promoting safety and efficiency of the paymentsystem the Central Bank shall co-operate with Central Banksof other countries and with other relevant domestic or foreignauthorities.\n\nCHAPTER II\n\nSECURITIES ACCOUNTS\n\n(2) A securities account holder may exercise all the rightsthat comprise the security credited to his or her securitiesaccount, or designated securities account, subject to anyapplicable adverse claim :\n\nProvided however, a customer securities account holdermay deal with his or her securities account as provided inthis section only through a dealer direct participant authorizedto act in that customer\u2019s securities account :\n\nProvided further that, no remedy against the account holderwill be prejudiced where the exercise of rights under thissection is in breach of a contract or is otherwise in violationof the rights of any other person.\n\n6Payment and Settlement SystemsAct, No. 28 of 2005\n\n(3) All communications and payments relating to asecurities account shall be submitted or made to or by theCentral Bank exclusively by or to\u2014\n\n(a)direct participants, in respect of own securitiesaccounts ; and\n\n(b)dealer direct participants, in respect of both ownaccounts and on securities accounts of their customersin respect of which they are authorized to act.\n\nEach disposition shall be recorded directly in the securitiesaccounts of the transferor and transferee of the security andnot pass through the own account of a dealer direct participantauthorized to act on behalf of a customer who is the transferoror transferee.\n\n(4) The provisions contained in this section shall be readconsistently with the provisions of the Local Treasury BillsOrdinance (Chapter 417) and the Registered Stocks andSecurities Ordinance (Chapter 420) respectively. Theprovisions contained in such Ordinances shall prevail in theevent of an inconsistency.\n\n7.(1) A disposition of a security is carried out by meansof debit and credit posted to the transferor\u2019s and transferee\u2019srespective securities account."
