    "chunk_text": "PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 1\n\nPrice : Rs. 4.25 Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of September 23, 2005\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Certified on 23rd September, 2005]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nSPORTS (AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 33 OF 2005\n\n1Sports (Amendment) Act, No. 33 of 2005\n\n[Certified on 23rd September, 2005]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 10/2005.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE SPORTS LAW, NO. 25 OF 1973\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Sports (Amendment)Act, No. 33 of 2005.\n\n2.Section 18 of the Sports Law, No. 25 of 1973(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended by the repeal of paragraph (b) of subseciton (2) ofthat section and the substitution therefor, of the followingparagraph :\u2014\n\n\u201c(b)members, if any of the International OlympicCommittee who are Sri Lankan Nationals, who shallbe ex-officio members.\u201d.\n\n3.Section 18A of the principal enactment is herebyreplaced and, the following section substituted therefor :\u2014\n\n18A. Every member of such Committee, otherthan the ex-officio members, shall hold officefor a term of four years.\u201d.\n\n4.Section 21 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the repeal of paragraph (e) of that section.\n\n5.In the event of any inconsistency between the SinhalaAnd Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendment ofsection 18 of theprincipalenactment.\n\nReplacement ofsection 18A of theprincipalenactment.\n\nAmendment ofsection 21of theprincipalenactment.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofany inconsistency.\n\n\u201cTerm ofoffice ofmembers ofCommittee.\n\nSports (Amendment) Act, No. 33 of 20052"
